    "['encapsulation source-address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing srv6', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing srv6\\n encapsulation source-address 5::5\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco's implementation of Segment Routing IPv6 (SRv6), the command structure is slightly different but achieves the same purpose of setting the source address for SRv6 encapsulation.\\n- The HUAWEI command `encapsulation source-address 5::5` under `segment-routing ipv6` context translates to Cisco's `encapsulation source-address 5::5` under `segment-routing srv6` configuration mode.\\n- Both commands specify the IPv6 address (5::5 in this case) that will be used as the source for SRv6 encapsulated packets.\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing srv6'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation source-address 5::5', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing srv6\\n encapsulation source-address 5::5\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco's implementation of Segment Routing IPv6 (SRv6), the command structure is slightly different but achieves the same purpose of setting the source address for SRv6 encapsulation.\\n- The HUAWEI command `encapsulation source-address 5::5` under `segment-routing ipv6` context translates to Cisco's `encapsulation source-address 5::5` under `segment-routing srv6` configuration mode.\\n- Both commands specify the IPv6 address (5::5 in this case) that will be used as the source for SRv6 encapsulated packets.\", 'trans_template': 'encapsulation source-address 5::5'}]]": 1,
    "['locator [parameter1] ipv6-prefix [parameter2] [parameter3] static [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `locator as1 ipv6-prefix` command is translated to Cisco's `segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix`\\n- The prefix (2001:db8:15::) and length (64) remain the same\\n- The static SID range (32) is kept identical\\n- The command maintains the same functionality of defining an SRv6 locator with a specific prefix and static SID allocation range\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid absolute 1 end', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid absolute 1 end\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command creates a static SID (Segment Identifier) with value 1 and marks it as an \"end\" segment (similar to a prefix-SID in Cisco)\\n- In Cisco, we use `prefix-sid absolute` to assign a static SID value\\n- The `end` keyword is maintained as it indicates this is an endpoint segment\\n- The locator name (`as1`) is preserved from the original configuration context\\n- The IPv6 SR configuration context is assumed to be already entered (just like in the Huawei config)', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid absolute 1 end'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end-dt4 vpn-instance [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid 100 end-dt4 vrf vpna', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix 2001:db8:15::/64 static 32'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid 100 end-dt4 vrf vpna\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::100 end-dt4 vpn-instance vpna` command under the SRv6 locator configuration:\\n  - Defines a SID (::100) for End.DT4 function (IPv4 VPN decapsulation)\\n  - Associates it with VPN instance \"vpna\"\\n- The Cisco equivalent:\\n  - Uses `prefix-sid` instead of `opcode`\\n  - Uses `vrf` instead of `vpn-instance`\\n  - Maintains the same SID value (100) and function (end-dt4)\\n  - The command is placed under the SRv6 locator configuration context', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid 100 end-dt4 vrf vpna'}]]": 1,
